   "batch": false,
   "comment": "value = base_value(elsewhere) + Sum_channels( affinity(x) * (state(a)+bias(c)) * gain(c) * pathway_gain(c) ), written ONCE, with the channel set as DATA (AffectChannel rows, has_affect_channel edges off c) -- a new channel is a new row, not a rule edit. Every read is P0-guarded: an UNTAGGED x (no affinity_* attr matching a channel's affinity_key) gets affect_bias==0.0 exactly, the vmPFC-lesion case as an absence, not a branch. Consumers opt in by (a) getting a couples_affect_to edge and (b) carrying affinity_* attrs -- nothing else.",
